# API contracts

This project uses the `openapi` contract mode. The committed source of truth is `contracts/openapi.json`.

Generate runtime-free TypeScript contract types with:

```bash
pnpm foundation:contract
```

Verify generated output and the contract lock with:

```bash
pnpm foundation:contract:verify
```

Generated types are intentionally transport-agnostic. Runtime HTTP requests continue to use `@foundation/api`, preserving Foundation `AppError`, timeout/cancellation, authentication injection, request IDs, and trace semantics.

`@hey-api/openapi-ts` is pinned exactly because the upstream package is pre-1.0. In Frontend Foundation 0.10 this adapter is Candidate and OpenAPI 3.1 is the only enabled specification line. OpenAPI 3.0 is blocked due to a known upstream parser correctness case; 3.2 remains an evaluation target until the real upstream fixture gate passes.

The adapter is an implementation detail and may be replaced without changing application runtime contracts.

0.10 Candidate accepts local committed JSON input only; YAML stays blocked until the upstream dependency security gate passes.
